    "note": "Snapshot, not a forecast series. Expected return = dividend yield (MSCI, gross vs price return over the last 12 months) + real growth (1.5 % for every region, a prudent long-run assumption) + expected inflation (Cleveland Fed 10-year for USD regions; 1.0 % assumed for CHF). The reversion column adds the annual effect of the CAPE moving to the reference level over 10 years (hand-entered quarterly). Outside the US buybacks are smaller, so the dividend yield captures most of the cash returned; for the US it understates it — see the FCF-based card above for the US. A Gordon test per country on 1870-2020 data did not validate well outside the US, hence no historical lines here. CHF view for USD regions: unhedged = relative PPP (CHF appreciates by the USD-CHF inflation gap); hedged = minus the cost of a rolling USD→CHF hedge, proxied by the US-CH 10-year yield gap. Personal use; MSCI data are not redistributed, only derived figures shown."
