    "note": "IWVL tracks the MSCI World Enhanced Value Index — a concentrated selection of the ~400 highest-value-scoring names out of the ~1,500-name MSCI World universe, cap-weighted within that selection. This is NOT the same as the MSCI World Value Weighted Index, which re-weights the full MSCI World universe by value score rather than selecting a subset — the two can diverge meaningfully. SWDA (iShares Core MSCI World) is the standard cap-weighted parent index used here as the benchmark."
